abstract: >
  We present Y1.3, a training-time use of a decoupled failure-prediction
  Monitor as a reward penalty for PPO. On LunarLander-v3 across 15 random
  seeds, Y1.3 produces a mean eval return of 80.1 +/- 45.9 vs the PPO
  baseline's 40.6 +/- 37.1 (t=6.76, df=14, p<0.001). We complement this
  with a 9-hypothesis pre-registered framework that maps the broader
  Monitor-in-RL research space. Of 9 hypotheses: 6 are VALIDATED, 2 are
  REFUTED, 1 is OPEN. A key negative finding: Y1.3 does NOT transfer to
  multi-agent (H5 REFUTED). The architectural lesson: Monitors are
  VERIFIERS, not reward signals. DLR cross-environment validation
  (97.8% mean over 4 envs) and the V1 governance evidence chain are the
  shipping uses.
